# finishTest appends the WebGL postlude without waiting for script loading

Firefox repository `git:314d8065c5ad68c7e5c5f92d`, revision `1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b`. Scope: DOM Canvas WebGL conformance tests and the shared Mochitest harness. Languages in the cited files: JavaScript. File roles are listed in the metadata. No production WebGL implementation is claimed.

finishTest sets successfullyParsed=true, creates a script element, scans script URLs for one ending exactly in js-test-pre.js, derives its directory or keeps an empty base path, then appends js-test-post.js to the body. It returns without waiting for that script to load.

## Caller and change impact

The dedicated `always-fail.html` sentinel calls `finishTest`. The representative inactive-attribute target loads `js-test-post.js` directly instead. Changing dynamic path resolution can affect the first route without proving an effect on the second.

**Ownership:** The target document owns the new script and DOM state. No onload/onerror listener, cancellation token, removal, or cleanup is registered here.

**Scope limit:** Some targets, including the inspected representative, load js-test-post directly instead. A template match does not establish which target entry path applies.

## Evidence

[`dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/js/js-test-pre.js` — `finishTest`, lines 776–792](https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/blob/1a097ed8d31f6b307a5d0ebc34a82ceaf7f3727b/dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/checkout/js/js-test-pre.js#L776-L792). Exact excerpt from lines 776–792:

```javascript
function finishTest() {
  successfullyParsed = true;
  var epilogue = document.createElement("script");
  var basePath = "";
  var expectedBase = "js-test-pre.js";
  var scripts = document.getElementsByTagName('script');
  for (var script, i = 0; script = scripts[i]; i++) {
    var src = script.src;
    var l = src.length;
    if (src.substr(l - expectedBase.length) == expectedBase) {
      basePath = src.substr(0, l - expectedBase.length);
      break;
    }
  }
  epilogue.src = basePath + "js-test-post.js";
  document.body.appendChild(epilogue);
}
```

## Test links and validation

**Direct source-defined check, narrow scope:** The [always-fail sentinel](3a5b3b5d-3324-4080-9187-3196bf4a7aed.md) checks the deliberately failed assertion route. Other forwarding details, duplicate completion, async cleanup, and preference restoration are not directly asserted by this sentinel. **Execution-only:** The [inactive-attribute target](09ff632c-c5e0-445c-a5de-440fb21349eb.md) enters the shared harness. Other possible test links remain unverified.

The cited implementation, callers, and applicable receiver bodies were read. An independent source review accepted this scoped relationship with its listed gaps. No Firefox or Thunderbird product tests, generator run, or build ran for this evidence. There is no runtime pass/fail result. No Thunderbird–Firefox call chain is added by this Firefox-only slice.

